id: nsq.flag.coverage.standard.v1
type: manifest
version: 1
authority: Braxon
role: flag_coverage_standard

purpose:
  NSQ must support every meaningful flag surface another language, toolchain, runtime,
  platform, renderer, package manager, or service stack exposes.

core_rule:
  foreign flag spelling is projection only
  native flag meaning is sovereign
  repeated flag patterns should collapse into stamps and cached execution plans

hard_laws:
  - No foreign flag meaning may remain inaccessible just because its original syntax differs.
  - Flat string-flag authority is forbidden.
  - Every flag must map to native semantic classes.
  - Projection back into foreign spellings is allowed.
  - Projection must not outrank native meaning.
  - Repeated flag bundles should become stamps.
  - Package and platform flag resolution should be cacheable and replayable.

required_flag_families:
  - build_compile
  - package_dependency
  - link_archive_artifact
  - runtime_launch_env
  - profile_debug_trace
  - test_verify_replay
  - platform_target_abi
  - android_device
  - render_asset_shader_scene
  - storage_db_migration_config
  - security_policy_permission
  - network_queue_stream_registry
  - projection_translation_export
